" d="M0 96C0 60.7 28.7 32 64 32H384c35.3 0 64 28.7 64 64V416c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V96z"></path></svg> Upgrade Materials</div><div class="info-box"><p><strong class="Electro">Hsin</strong> <strong>upgrade material information aren't available yet.</strong></p></div><div class="content-header Electro"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="square" class="svg-inline--fa fa-square" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 96C0 60.7 28.7 32 64 32H384c35.3 0 64 28.7 64 64V416c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V96z"></path></svg> Voice Actors</div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg-1420:grid-cols-4 gap-6 va-section"><div class="flex-1"><div class="info-list-row"><div class="category">ENG</div><div class="details">-</div></div></div><div class="flex-1"><div class="info-list-row"><div class="category">JPN</div><div class="details">-</div></div></div><div class="flex-1"><div class="info-list-row"><div class="category">CN</div><div class="details">-</div></div></div><div class="flex-1"><div class="info-list-row"><div class="category">KR</div><div class="details">-</div></div></div></div><div class="content-header Electro"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="square" class="svg-inline--fa fa-square" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 96C0 60.7 28.7 32 64 32H384c35.3 0 64 28.7 64 64V416c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V96z"></path></svg> Gallery</div><img alt="Hsin" loading="lazy" width="600" height="750" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="full-image" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/hsin_full.webp" style="color: transparent;"></div><div class="tab-inside "><div class="mobile-header Electro"><p><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="circle-info" class="svg-inline--fa fa-circle-info" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 512 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M256 512A256 256 0 1 0 256 0a256 256 0 1 0 0 512zM216 336l24 0 0-64-24 0c-13.3 0-24-10.7-24-24s10.7-24 24-24l48 0c13.3 0 24 10.7 24 24l0 88 8 0c13.3 0 24 10.7 24 24s-10.7 24-24 24l-80 0c-13.3 0-24-10.7-24-24s10.7-24 24-24zm40-208a32 32 0 1 1 0 64 32 32 0 1 1 0-64z"></path></svg> Review</p></div><div class="content-header Electro"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="square" class="svg-inline--fa fa-square" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 96C0 60.7 28.7 32 64 32H384c35.3 0 64 28.7 64 64V416c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V96z"></path></svg> Ratings</div><div class="info-box tier"><p>Please keep in mind Wuthering Waves is a skill-based game and each character has a different playstyle, difficulty level and even special tricks and combos. Wuthering Waves is also a team based game and it's only by combining both these factors to the highest level a character can reach optimal performance.</p></div><div><h5><span class="role dps"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="hand-fist" class="svg-inline--fa fa-hand-fist" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="12"><path fill="currentColor" d="M192 0c17.7 0 32 14.3 32 32l0 112-64 0 0-112c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32zM64 64c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32s32 14.3 32 32l0 80-64 0 0-80zm192 0c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32s32 14.3 32 32l0 96c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32s-32-14.3-32-32l0-96zm96 64c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32s32 14.3 32 32l0 64c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32s-32-14.3-32-32l0-64zm-96 88l0-.6c9.4 5.4 20.3 8.6 32 8.6c13.2 0 25.4-4 35.6-10.8c8.7 24.9 32.5 42.8 60.4 42.8c11.7 0 22.6-3.1 32-8.6l0 8.6c0 52.3-25.1 98.8-64 128l0 96c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32l-160 0c-17.7 0-32-14.3-32-32l0-78.4c-17.3-7.9-33.2-18.8-46.9-32.5L69.5 357.5C45.5 333.5 32 300.9 32 267l0-27c0-35.3 28.7-64 64-64l88 0c22.1 0 40 17.9 40 40s-17.9 40-40 40l-56 0c-8.8 0-16 7.2-16 16s7.2 16 16 16l56 0c39.8 0 72-32.2 72-72z"></path></svg> DPS<span class="role-dupes"> [S0]</span></span></h5><div class="detailed-ratings ww"><div class="rating-box-container "><span><div class="rating-box ww T0-5">T0.5</div></span><p>Tower of Adversity</p></div><div class="rating-box-container "><span><div class="rating-box ww T1">T1</div></span><p>Whimpering Wastes</p></div></div></div><h6 class="text-lg value-tier-heading">Value Tier List</h6><div><h5><span class="role dps"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="hand-fist" class="svg-inline--fa fa-hand-fist" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="12"><path fill="currentColor" d="M192 0c17.7 0 32 14.3 32 32l0 112-64 0 0-112c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32zM64 64c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32s32 14.3 32 32l0 80-64 0 0-80zm192 0c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32s32 14.3 32 32l0 96c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32s-32-14.3-32-32l0-96zm96 64c0-17.7 14.3-32 32-32s32 14.3 32 32l0 64c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32s-32-14.3-32-32l0-64zm-96 88l0-.6c9.4 5.4 20.3 8.6 32 8.6c13.2 0 25.4-4 35.6-10.8c8.7 24.9 32.5 42.8 60.4 42.8c11.7 0 22.6-3.1 32-8.6l0 8.6c0 52.3-25.1 98.8-64 128l0 96c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32l-160 0c-17.7 0-32-14.3-32-32l0-78.4c-17.3-7.9-33.2-18.8-46.9-32.5L69.5 357.5C45.5 333.5 32 300.9 32 267l0-27c0-35.3 28.7-64 64-64l88 0c22.1 0 40 17.9 40 40s-17.9 40-40 40l-56 0c-8.8 0-16 7.2-16 16s7.2 16 16 16l56 0c39.8 0 72-32.2 72-72z"></path></svg> DPS<span class="role-dupes"> [S0]</span></span></h5><div class="detailed-ratings ww"><div class="rating-box-container "><span><div class="rating-box ww T0-5">T0.5</div></span><p>Tower of Adversity (Value)</p></div><div class="rating-box-container "><span><div class="rating-box ww T1">T1</div></span><p>Whimpering Wastes (Value)</p></div></div></div><div class="content-header Electro"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="square" class="svg-inline--fa fa-square" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 96C0 60.7 28.7 32 64 32H384c35.3 0 64 28.7 64 64V416c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V96z"></path></svg> Pros &amp; Cons</div><div class="section-analysis"><div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 pros-cons"><div class="box pros"><h5 class="text-xl">Pros</h5><hr><div class="rte-plain raw list"><ul><li><p>The new best Electro DPS (pretty rare thing to say as Electro damage dealers are hard to come by);</p></li><li><p>Has access to very F2P-friendly team compositions in Flare mode - will essentially never be stranded for teammates, even for beginners;</p></li><li><p>Has significant room to grow as a DPS as Unison becomes a more developed character archetype.</p></li></ul><p></p></div></div><div class="box cons"><h5 class="text-xl">Cons</h5><hr><div class="rte-plain raw list"><ul><li><p>Pretty underwhelming Sequences in Flare mode aside from her S6 - has standard sequence values in Unison mode though;</p></li><li><p>Permanent banner weapon options are underwhelming; generally try to go for her Signature if youâ€™re pulling her;</p></li><li><p>â€œBrings Jinhsi back into the meta via Unison modeâ€ is what weâ€™d like to say, but in truth, Hsinâ€™s full F2P Electro Flare team is just as good as her full premium Unison team with Jinhsi. No reason to bring Jinhsi back despite Hsinâ€™s access to Coordinated Attacks and Unison-related synergies.</p></li></ul><p></p></div></div></div></div><div class="content-header Electro"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="square" class="svg-inline--fa fa-square" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 96C0 60.7 28.7 32 64 32H384c35.3 0 64 28.7 64 64V416c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V96z"></path></svg> Review</div><div class="section-analysis"><div class="rte-plain review raw"><p>Hsin is a 5-star Electro Rectifier Main DPS who plays into the Electro Flare archetype and a (sort of) brand new one, Unison. Electro Flare is one of the many Negative Statuses, and all of them have received significant attention meta-wise recently. However, Unison is a previously forgotten mechanic only Jinhsi possessed up until now, that involves your character doing 2 Outros per rotation: Unison gives one for free, and your Concerto gauge gives you the other. In the same vein as how Jinhsi plays, this creates more unique team rotations compared to the usual. With that being said, Hsinâ€™s kit has many complex elements based on her Resonance Mode, so weâ€™ll have to go in-depth to fully understand it.</p><p><strong><u>Key Mechanics &amp; Rotation Concepts</u></strong></p><p>Hsin has 3 states that she will switch between during battle throughout her rotation: Answering Form, Illumining Form, and Mechanism Dominion. In Answering Form, you build up the Forte required to switch to Illumining Form, then in that form, you build up the Forte that is required to enter Mechanism Dominion, at which point you consume said Forte to then unleash Hsinâ€™s final Ultimate. Pretty straightforward idea.</p><p>However, we can go a bit more in-depth on the details here, based on Hsinâ€™s resonance mode. They fundamentally change how she will rotate and what kinds of synergies she will get.</p><p>In Electro Flare mode, Hsin will perform a standard 1-2-3 team rotation like in any classic team youâ€™ve previously played, so sheâ€™ll do her on-field rotation fully until her Outro is ready and all her key abilities have been cast. Flare mechanics work in this way:</p><ul><li><p>Electro Flare stacks normally get consumed every time the instance of periodic damage it should deal is triggered. When Hsin is on the team, this is not the case. Instead, Hsin will have any extra Electro Flare stacks over the stack limit (10 at base) converted into Heart of Thunder instead of Electro Rage, to then unleash a detonation of its damage in one Skill.</p></li><li><p>Electro Flare is applied by: Her first Ultimate, Forte Skill, her Basics after her Forte Skill, and her second Forte Heavy (5 stacks each), as well as her Intro (1 stack).</p></li><li><p>Once Hsin casts her first Ultimate, she will apply 1 stack of Electro Flare to enemies who have none. If another teammate applies at least 10 Flare, Hsin stores this information and raises the Flare count up to the max instead. These effects apply to all nearby enemies until her rotation ends.</p></li><li><p>Hsin gains extra Electro DMG Bonus when another character in the team applies Electro Flare onto enemies, with an extra boost if that character is Electro Rover.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p>In Unison mode, Hsin rotates quite differently. Unison provides her with a free Outro once every 25s when her first Ultimate is cast, at the cost of no Concerto energy. Other mechanics include:</p><ul><li><p>Hsin increases the DMG of all Unison Response characters, including herself, by stacking up a unique buff (somewhat similar to Tune Strain) called Unison Boon. This buff is given when Unison Response characters perform Intros with each other;</p></li><li><p>Hsin can entirely skip the Illumining Form state and go straight into Mechanism Dominion if she Intros again after her First Ultimate;</p></li><li><p>Hsinâ€™s Intros are enhanced if they are triggered by another Unison character and they give Hsin 50% more ATK for 8s.</p></li></ul><p>In other words, you are heavily incentivized to use Unison mode with and only with other Unison characters. To add to this, Hsinâ€™s Outro gives 20% DMG amplification to other characters in the team than herself, but only to Electro DMG (Electro Flare mode) or Unison characters (Unison mode).</p><p>Hence, we can conclude Hsinâ€™s rotation will have her stacking up her Forte gauges (which she can only do while she is active on the field, so Swap Cancelling is restricted) and entering Illumining Form via her Ultimate. In Unison mode, she will switch out until another Unison character can give her another Intro. In Flare mode, she will stay on field and charge up her second Forte, both things done to enter Mechanism Dominion state, at which point she can do a few Basic Attacks to consume the Forte, cast her second Forte Heavy and Ultimate, and then Outro until her next rotation starts.</p><p><strong><u>Meta Position &amp; Conclusion</u></strong></p><p>You may have guessed the following when we described the Unison state mechanics:&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>Electro Flare is Hsinâ€™s more flexible mode teammates-wise, and her most F2P-friendly.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Currently, the only Unison character available is Jinhsi, and she cannot fully activate all the buffs in Hsinâ€™s kit. Not to mention, the team is rather weak compared to the rest of the current meta. In other words, new teammates are to come for this Resonance Mode.</p></li></ul><p>And this is entirely true. Performance-wise, Hsinâ€™s Flare teams are however still restricted to using Electro Rover and Suisui at best outside of Quickswap (where Chisa would be privileged instead). Overall, Electro Rover is far from an ideal character, with low total buffing potential and a lengthy rotation, meaning they too could be replaced in the future. But for now, they are enough to make Hsin a good DPS still, and a budget-friendly one at that, able to run Buling in the 3rd slot for a nearly cost-free team composition while still retaining good enough performance to clear endgame modes when played properly.</p><p>For this reason though, raw performance-wise, Hsin is below the rest of the modern 3.x cast. Luuk can expect to see a bit higher results than her too. With that being said, Hsin has a way out in the form of Unison Mode, which has not been expanded upon yet. We can expect Kuro to release more Unison characters to synergize with Hsin to bring her up to modern performance standards. With that being said, we have no guarantee of this, so right now Hsin is simply a more budget-friendly Flare DPS than the rest of the modern cast, being able to take advantage of Rover better than any other character currently, who is accessible to everyone and doesnâ€™t need their Signature weapon.&nbsp;</p><p>In conclusion, while Hsin has no good permanent banner weapons, with her and her Signature, you essentially have a guaranteed Flare team for her out of the box, and that makes her a great pull for beginner players. In the future, she may be subject to receiving additional firepower through Unison, but for now her performance ceiling is quite a bit below her peers. Keep this into account when choosing whether to pull for her or not.</p></div></div><div class="content-header Electro"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="square" class="svg-inline--fa fa-square" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 96C0 60.7 28.7 32 64 32H384c35.3 0 64 28.7 64 64V416c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V96z"></path></svg> Video guides</div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 video-row"><div class="flex-1"><div class="video-responsive"><button type="button" class="yt-facade" aria-label="Play video"><img alt="" fetchpriority="low" decoding="async" class="yt-facade-thumb" src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/5y0V5t-HYSo/maxresdefault.webp"><span class="yt-facade-play" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></div></div></div></div><div class="tab-inside "><div class="mobile-header Electro"><p><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="circle-info" class="svg-inline--fa fa-circle-info" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 512 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M256 512A256 256 0 1 0 256 0a256 256 0 1 0 0 512zM216 336l24 0 0-64-24 0c-13.3 0-24-10.7-24-24s10.7-24 24-24l48 0c13.3 0 24 10.7 24 24l0 88 8 0c13.3 0 24 10.7 24 24s-10.7 24-24 24l-80 0c-13.3