2.8-12.5 45.3 0s12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160zm160-352l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0l-160-160c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0L224 210.7 361.4 73.4c12.5-12.5 32.8-12.5 45.3 0s12.5 32.8 0 45.3z"></path></svg></div><div class="skill"><p>Res. Skill</p></div></div><p>Skill can be skipped when levelling to save on resources at a minimal damage loss. Basic is also lower-priority, but still worth levelling at endgame level.</p></div><div class="tab-inside active"><div class="mobile-header Electro"><p><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="people-group" class="svg-inline--fa fa-people-group" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 640 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M72 88a56 56 0 1 1 112 0A56 56 0 1 1 72 88zM64 245.7C54 256.9 48 271.8 48 288s6 31.1 16 42.3l0-84.7zm144.4-49.3C178.7 222.7 160 261.2 160 304c0 34.3 12 65.8 32 90.5l0 21.5c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32l-64 0c-17.7 0-32-14.3-32-32l0-26.8C26.2 371.2 0 332.7 0 288c0-61.9 50.1-112 112-112l32 0c24 0 46.2 7.5 64.4 20.3zM448 416l0-21.5c20-24.7 32-56.2 32-90.5c0-42.8-18.7-81.3-48.4-107.7C449.8 183.5 472 176 496 176l32 0c61.9 0 112 50.1 112 112c0 44.7-26.2 83.2-64 101.2l0 26.8c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32l-64 0c-17.7 0-32-14.3-32-32zm8-328a56 56 0 1 1 112 0A56 56 0 1 1 456 88zM576 245.7l0 84.7c10-11.3 16-26.1 16-42.3s-6-31.1-16-42.3zM320 32a64 64 0 1 1 0 128 64 64 0 1 1 0-128zM240 304c0 16.2 6 31 16 42.3l0-84.7c-10 11.3-16 26.1-16 42.3zm144-42.3l0 84.7c10-11.3 16-26.1 16-42.3s-6-31.1-16-42.3zM448 304c0 44.7-26.2 83.2-64 101.2l0 42.8c0 17.7-14.3 32-32 32l-64 0c-17.7 0-32-14.3-32-32l0-42.8c-37.8-18-64-56.5-64-101.2c0-61.9 50.1-112 112-112l32 0c61.9 0 112 50.1 112 112z"></path></svg> Gameplay and teams</p></div><div class="content-header Electro"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="square" class="svg-inline--fa fa-square" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 96C0 60.7 28.7 32 64 32H384c35.3 0 64 28.7 64 64V416c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V96z"></path></svg> Rotation</div><div class="section-analysis"><div class="rte-plain review raw"><h5 id="rotation--how-to-play"><strong><u>Rotation &amp; How to Play</u></strong></h5><p>Hsinâ€™s rotation is fundamentally easy to understand: build up her Forte to cast her first Forte Heavy Attack, this unlocks her Ultimate. Then, enter Mechanism Dominion and finish it off with her second Forte Heavy Attack and Ultimate. She has two ways to achieve this, based on her Resonance Mode that changes her rotation.</p><div class="callout callout-info " data-callout="" data-callout-type="info" style="--callout-color: #3B82F6;"><div class="callout-header"><span class="callout-icon" aria-hidden="true">â„¹ï¸</span><span class="callout-title">Info</span></div><div class="callout-content"><div class="callout-icon" data-icon="circle-info"></div><div class="callout-content"><h6 id="echo-timing">Echo Timing</h6><p>Summon Hsinâ€™s Echo freely at any point throughout her rotation.</p></div></div></div><h6 id="electro-flare-rotation"><strong><u>Electro Flare Rotation</u></strong></h6><p>In Electro Flare mode, Hsin will adopt a standard 1-2-3 team rotation the same way the majority of the DPS characters in the game have up until this point. To use all of her key abilities the quickest, we can execute the following rotation:</p><ul><li><p>Intro</p></li><li><p>Basic 4</p></li><li><p>Heavy: Realm Protector</p></li><li><p>Ultimate: Formshift</p></li><li><p>Skill: Illumining</p></li><li><p>Basic: Illumining 1</p></li><li><p>Basic: Illumining 2 (Cancel animation endlag via Skill)</p></li><li><p>Skill: Pillars</p></li><li><p>Basic: Pillars 1</p></li><li><p>Basic: Pillars 2</p></li><li><p>Basic: Pillars 3</p></li><li><p>Basic: Pillars 4</p></li><li><p>Heavy: Stilling All Horizons</p></li><li><p>Ultimate: Pillars Across Heaven</p></li><li><p>Skill (Swap)</p></li><li><p>Outro</p></li></ul><h6 id="unison-rotation"><strong><u>Unison Rotation</u></strong></h6><p>In Unison mode, Hsinâ€™s team rotation concept changes to be similar to what Jinhsi used to offer in the past. Here, going by Intros and Outros as reference points, itâ€™s more of a 1-2-3-2-3 loop, where 1 is your Support, 2 is your Unison secondary, and 3 is Hsin herself. She will indeed use 2 Intros per rotation to skip any Illumining Form attacks and go straight into Mechanism Dominion with the extra perk of retaining the maximum amount of damage buffs possible, like so:</p><ul><li><p>Intro: Manifold Unison</p></li><li><p>Basic 3</p></li><li><p>Basic 4</p></li><li><p>Heavy: Realm Protector</p></li><li><p>Ultimate: Formshift</p></li><li><p>Outro (Unison)</p></li></ul><p><em>â€”&gt; Build up a second Outro from your Unison Secondary here.</em></p><ul><li><p>Intro: Manifold Unison</p></li><li><p>Basic: Pillars 1</p></li><li><p>Basic: Pillars 2</p></li><li><p>Basic: Pillars 3</p></li><li><p>Basic: Pillars 4</p></li><li><p>Heavy: Stilling All Horizons</p></li><li><p>Ultimate: Pillars Across Heaven&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Skill (Swap)</p></li><li><p>Outro</p></li></ul><p></p></div></div><div class="content-header Electro"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="square" class="svg-inline--fa fa-square" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 96C0 60.7 28.7 32 64 32H384c35.3 0 64 28.7 64 64V416c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V96z"></path></svg> Synergies</div><ul class="bigger-margin"><li><span aria-expanded="false"><a class="inline-character-ww rarity-5" href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/rover-electro"><span class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Rover (Electro)" loading="lazy" width="60" height="60" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/rover-electro_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></span><span class="inline-name">Rover (Electro)</span></a></span> <span aria-expanded="false"><a class="inline-character-ww rarity-5" href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/jinhsi"><span class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Jinhsi" loading="lazy" width="60" height="60" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/jinhsi_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></span><span class="inline-name">Jinhsi</span></a></span> - <span>Electro Rover is Hsin's current best second slot teammate, as they provide her with some external Electro Flare application which is great for triggering her passives, as well as being able to provide her with a massive amount of Electro DMG Bonus among some other buffs. Jinhsi is the only current Unison character in the game, so she's the only option for Unison mode Hsin to be used with normally, but generally she's not recommended even over a F2P Flare team.</span></li><li><span aria-expanded="false"><a class="inline-character-ww rarity-5" href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/the-shorekeeper"><span class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="The Shorekeeper" loading="lazy" width="60" height="60" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/the-shorekeeper_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></span><span class="inline-name">The Shorekeeper</span></a></span> <span aria-expanded="false"><a class="inline-character-ww rarity-5" href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/suisui"><span class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Suisui" loading="lazy" width="60" height="60" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/suisui_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></span><span class="inline-name">Suisui</span></a></span> <span aria-expanded="false"><a class="inline-character-ww rarity-5" href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/chisa"><span class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Chisa" loading="lazy" width="60" height="60" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/chisa_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></span><span class="inline-name">Chisa</span></a></span> <span aria-expanded="false"><a class="inline-character-ww rarity-4" href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/buling"><span class="avatar ww rarity-4"><img alt="Buling" loading="lazy" width="60" height="60" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/buling_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></span><span class="inline-name">Buling</span></a></span> - <span>Shorekeeper is Unison Hsin's best current Support as there is no dedicated Support for Unison teams, so she comes out on top by virtue of being the best generalist choice. Suisui, Chisa and Buling are all options for Electro Flare Hsin. Suisui is generally the strongest, but Chisa can outperform her in Quickswap. Buling is the F2P fallback option, giving extra Flare application and Skill DMG-oriented buffs.</span></li></ul><div class="content-header Electro"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="square" class="svg-inline--fa fa-square" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 96C0 60.7 28.7 32 64 32H384c35.3 0 64 28.7 64 64V416c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V96z"></path></svg> Example Teams</div><div class="team-showcase box Electro"><div class="team-header"><p>Best Team (Flare)</p></div><div class="team-row"><div class="column "><div class="big"><span aria-expanded="false"><a href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/hsin"><div class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Hsin" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition character-icon-responsive" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/hsin_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></div></a></span></div><div class="small"></div></div><div class="column middle"><div class="big"><span aria-expanded="false"><a href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/rover-electro"><div class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Rover (Electro)" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition character-icon-responsive" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/rover-electro_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></div></a></span></div><div class="small"></div></div><div class="column "><div class="big"><span aria-expanded="false"><a href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/suisui"><div class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Suisui" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition character-icon-responsive" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/suisui_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></div></a></span></div><div class="small"><span aria-expanded="false"><a href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/chisa"><div class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Chisa" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition character-icon-responsive" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/chisa_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></div></a></span><span aria-expanded="false"><a href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/buling"><div class="avatar ww rarity-4"><img alt="Buling" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition character-icon-responsive" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/buling_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></div></a></span></div></div></div><div class="team-notes"><p>By way of more flexibility in quickswap, Chisa could prove stronger for more experienced players willing to take advantage of the mechanic.</p></div><div class="team-header"><p>Best Team (Unison)</p></div><div class="team-row"><div class="column "><div class="big"><span aria-expanded="false"><a href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/hsin"><div class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Hsin" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition character-icon-responsive" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/hsin_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></div></a></span></div><div class="small"></div></div><div class="column middle"><div class="big"><span aria-expanded="false"><a href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/jinhsi"><div class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Jinhsi" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition character-icon-responsive" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/jinhsi_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></div></a></span></div><div class="small"></div></div><div class="column "><div class="big"><span aria-expanded="false"><a href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/the-shorekeeper"><div class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="The Shorekeeper" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition character-icon-responsive" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/the-shorekeeper_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></div></a></span></div><div class="small"><span aria-expanded="false"><a href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/verina"><div class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Verina" loading="lazy" width="120" height="120" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="disable-transition character-icon-responsive" src="https://cdn.prydwen.gg/images/wuthering-waves/characters/verina_icon.webp" style="color: transparent;"></div></a></span></div></div></div><div class="team-notes"><p>Generally never recommended unless you really want to make use of Unison Hsin or Jinhsi, delivers very similar performance to Electro Rover + Buling in a Flare team.</p></div></div></div><div class="tab-inside "><div class="mobile-header Electro"><p><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="circle-info" class="svg-inline--fa fa-circle-info" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 512 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M256 512A256 256 0 1 0 256 0a256 256 0 1 0 0 512zM216 336l24 0 0-64-24 0c-13.3 0-24-10.7-24-24s10.7-24 24-24l48 0c13.3 0 24 10.7 24 24l0 88 8 0c13.3 0 24 10.7 24 24s-10.7 24-24 24l-80 0c-13.3 0-24-10.7-24-24s10.7-24 24-24zm40-208a32 32 0 1 1 0 64 32 32 0 1 1 0-64z"></path></svg> Calculations</p></div><div class="content-header Electro"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-prefix="fas" data-icon="square" class="svg-inline--fa fa-square" role="img" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" width="18"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 96C0 60.7 28.7 32 64 32H384c35.3 0 64 28.7 64 64V416c0 35.3-28.7 64-64 64H64c-35.3 0-64-28.7-64-64V96z"></path></svg> Damage Output</div><div class="pw-alert relative p-4 mb-4 rounded border pw-alert-primary pw-alert-red" role="alert"><p><strong>Don't use the damage output calculations as an indication on who is worth pulling or investing</strong> as those are just simulations and in day-to-day gameplay there's a lot variables and also the skill of the player is important - if you can't consistently perform the character's rotation, their damage will suffer.</p><p>As usual, <strong>don't compare the numbers between characters</strong> - especially between Main DPS and Hybrids as they fulfill different roles in the team.</p></div><h5>Additional information</h5><p>The numbers below show the character's <strong>DPS (Damage Per Second) and DMG (total damage done)</strong>. When selecting the rotations we prioritized achieving 100 Concerto as fast as possible and once that condition was fulfilled, we focused on maximizing the damage output. As or if new and more optimal rotations are found, we'll update the characters calculations as needed. Listed character calculations are done without buffs or any damage contribution from teammates (full solo). They only include what the character, their Weapon, Echo and gear are capable of during their ideal Burst or Concerto rotation when starting with their Intro and Resonance Liberation available.</p><p><strong>Do note that DPS and DMG aren't perfect metrics for a character's individual value and should be taken with a grain of salt.</strong> Anything pertaining a character's relevance in the meta is addressed in our Review and Tier List, which the numbers below shouldn't be used for as an end-all-be-all to. Instead, DPS and DMG are good metrics for a character's sequence value and comparison between an individual character's different rotations. We recommend using those metrics for such purposes.</p><div class="tabs-calcs" role="tablist" aria-label="Calculation sets" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0px, 1fr));"><div id="calc-hsin-tab-0" class="single-tab Electro active" role="tab" tabindex="0" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="calc-hsin-panel-0"><p>Unison</p></div><div id="calc-hsin-tab-1" class="single-tab Electro " role="tab" tabindex="-1" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="calc-hsin-panel-1"><p>Electro Flare</p></div></div><div id="calc-hsin-panel-0" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="calc-hsin-tab-0"><h6>Calculations information</h6><p>The calculations were done using added buffs from the following teammates:</p><ul class="bigger-margin"><li><span aria-expanded="false"><a class="inline-character-ww rarity-5" href="https://www.prydwen.gg/wuthering-waves/characters/jinhsi"><span class="avatar ww rarity-5"><img alt="Jinhsi" loading="lazy" width="60" height="60" de